      "body": "## SaveVault v1.0.0\r\n\r\nBack up your game saves to your own Google Drive. Never lose a save again.\r\n\r\n### What's included\r\n- Sign in with Google \u2014 your saves go directly to your own Drive, nothing else\r\n- Add any number of games with custom names and local save paths\r\n- Full recursive sync \u2014 backs up all files and subfolders inside your save directory\r\n- Conflict resolution \u2014 if both sides changed, you choose which version wins\r\n- Restore on a new PC \u2014 sign in and sync back down automatically\r\n- Modern dark-themed UI, no installation required\r\n\r\n### How to use\r\n1. Download `SaveVault.exe` below\r\n2. Run it \u2014 no installation needed\r\n3. Sign in with your Google account\r\n4. Click **+ Add Game**, name it, and point it at your save folder\r\n5. Click **Sync**\r\n\r\n> If Google shows an \"unverified app\" warning, click **Advanced \u2192 Go to SaveVault (unsafe)**.\r\n> This is normal for apps that haven't gone through Google's review process yet \u2014 it is safe.\r\n\r\n### Want to build it yourself?\r\nDownload the source code and read `INSTRUCTIONS.txt` for a step-by-step guide to\r\nbuilding SaveVault with your own Google Cloud credentials.\r\n\r\n### Requirements\r\n- Windows 10 or 11 (64-bit)\r\n- A Google account"
